AB  - Critiquing expert systems differ from conventional expert systems in that system users input a proposed plan of action. The critiquing expert system provides constructive comments on the proposed plan as well as alternatives to it. This approach has two advantages over conventional expert systems: (1) users retain their authority over decision making and are not “deskilled,” and (2) complex planning and management tasks with many alternative “solutions” can be accommodated. A critiquing system developed to assist in managing the operations of the San Francisco Water Department illustrates the approach and its potential for assisting planners.
