KW  - Waste utilisation
KW  - Mable dust
KW  - Concrete
KW  - Physical properties
KW  - Scientometric review
AB  - The construction industry is one of the prime polluters of the global environment, in addition to the waste management menace. Over the years, waste marble dust reuse as aggregates has gained budding interest among researchers and practitioners in a diverse geographical setting as one of the ground-breaking practices integrating sustainable construction applications. However, a systematic scientometric study appraising the utilisation of waste marble dust in concrete applications remains elusive. This study intends to address this gap by performing a scientometric review of the existing documents on waste marble dust into sustainable concrete production in the Scopus database. By analysing accessible bibliometric data and finding associated document areas, sources with the most significant publications, the most often occurring keywords, scholars, and articles with the utmost citations. The scientometric analysis determines the current state of research on waste marble dust use in sustainable construction applications. The reported test conducted is discovered and discussed, the optimum proportions of percentage replacement of marble dust are determined, and the performance of other recycled aggregates with marble dust. In addition, knowledge gaps and future research directions were identified. This study adds to the motivation of in-depth knowledge in the reuse of waste marble dust in sustainable construction applications, provides a point of reference in bridging the gaps in the existing research and gives future directions for the study of marble dust.
