This chapter examines a broad set of challenging issues in the domain of mobile computing. It emphasizes on the design issues of the underlying heterogeneous networks. Mobile terminals such as smart phones are also considered when a network service is delivered to the end unit. With regard to wireless networks, it discusses network organization issues (heterogeneous network integration, mobile next-generation networks, and ad hoc networks), network service issues (QoS provision and routing protocols), and network transport (wireless TCP). The chapter illusyrates that, as wireless technologies continues to emerge with new applications and services, it is undoubtedly impossible to cover every aspect of the entire wireless arena. This chapter mainly focuses the utilization of fundamental computer networking techniques and methodologies. This chapter concludes that, as more and more mobile devices begin to invade our daily life and people become increasingly dependent on them, security and privacy issues are receiving tremendous attention from both academic researchers and industry practitioners.
